# Caching

- Cache read-heavy `GET` endpoints only with a TTL and a clear invalidation plan
- Never cache write endpoints without invalidation/update strategy
- Multi-instance: avoid in-memory cache for shared state; use Redis distributed cache
- Prefer cache-aside unless the use case demands write-through/write-behind

